  "reportReceiptHelp": "We’ll review your report and use it\nto improve the app.",
  "reportReceiptId": "Report ID",
  "reportDone": "Done",
  "privacyOverviewTitle": "Card information is normally processed on your device",
  "privacyOverviewBody": "Recent transit card records are read using NFC and displayed on screen. They are not retained after the app closes. The raw card IDm is used only temporarily during NFC communication and is not stored, displayed or transmitted.",
  "privacyNfcTitle": "1. Why we use NFC",
  "privacyNfcBody": "NFC permission is used to read records and identify the type of Japanese transit IC card when you start a scan. In a separate card recognition inquiry, only minimal metadata is checked with your consent. The app does not write to or modify your card.",
  "privacyOnDeviceTitle": "2. Information processed on your device",
  "privacyOnDeviceBody": "The app interprets and displays the original 16-byte records, dates, transaction types, station codes and names, amounts and balances from recent transactions on your device. Records are not stored permanently. Scanning another card in the normal scan flow replaces the current results.\n\nThe multiple-card balance comparison feature keeps the names, balances, check times and records of up to 10 cards only in the comparison screen’s memory. To distinguish cards, it uses a session-only comparison value created with a random key for each comparison session; the raw IDm is not retained. Comparison values, keys and card names are not saved to files or transmitted to a server. They are cleared when the comparison ends or the app process exits. Deleting an individual card also removes its comparison information. A comparison scan does not change the existing card results on the home screen.",
  "privacyReportsTitle": "3. Information sent with an issue report",
  "privacyReportsBody": "Issue reports are optional. Only after you review the preview and give your consent does the app send the selected transaction’s raw record, codes and interpreted information, date, amount and balance, the station, city, line or bus operator, operating city/region and description you enter, app, parser and station data versions, platform and OS version to Supabase. This information is used to improve the app.\n\nA separate card recognition inquiry is different from a transaction report. With your consent to a diagnostic scan, the app checks only system codes, manufacturer information (PMm), the presence of selected permitted services and communication error codes on your device. Only after you review the data, purpose and retention period and give separate, explicit consent are these minimal diagnostics, the card type and description you enter, app/OS versions, report ID and consent document version sent to Supabase. They are used to improve card identification and reading errors. A full card dump, service contents, balance and transaction history are not included in this inquiry. The app does not retain the inquiry contents after you leave the screen.",
  "privacyNotSentTitle": "4. Information not included in reports",
  "privacyNotSentBody": "The raw card IDm, other unselected transaction records, your name, email address, unique device identifiers, current location and travel route are not included in report data.",
  "privacyServicesTitle": "5. External processing services",
  "privacyServicesBody": "Issue reports use Supabase’s anonymous authentication, server and database services. An anonymous authentication ID is used only within the server to limit submissions to five per 10 minutes and block abusive reports. It is not an email address, card IDm or unique device ID. It is not shown in the app and is used with report information only on the access-restricted server. Reports are processed through Supabase infrastructure. Technical information associated with network connections may be processed under the service’s operating policies.",
  "privacyMapsTitle": "5-1. Google Maps",
  "privacyMapsBody": "When you open rail transaction details, a Google Maps SDK map is displayed automatically if the app confirms an internet connection, station locations and map configuration. Possible locations are shown for station groups and segments. The area around the stations and their coordinates are used in map requests. Google may process IP addresses, device, OS and SDK information, SDK-specific pseudonymous identifiers, diagnostics and usage information. The app does not request current-location permission or pass your card IDm, card number, balance or raw transaction records to the map SDK. Google’s Privacy Policy (https://policies.google.com/privacy) applies. If an internet connection cannot be confirmed, the map is not displayed; you can retry using Refresh map after connecting. Connection status is checked on your device using Android network capability information, without contacting a separate connectivity-check server. Stopping or refreshing a map does not cancel or delete requests already made. Card reading and the transaction list remain available without a map connection. The app does not separately store map usage history. Google’s retention and deletion rules are governed by its policies.",
  "privacyStationDataTitle": "6. Station code data",
  "privacyStationDataBody": "Station names are looked up using licensed Yoiko station code data bundled with the app. Lookups take place on your device; card records are not sent to an external server to identify station names. You can find the terms of use under Data sources and fare rules in Settings.",
  "privacyRetentionTitle": "7. Retention and deletion",
  "privacyRetentionBody": "The app does not permanently store records read from your card. Optional reports that have been applied or rejected, together with their review histories, are retained for one year after resolution and then deleted by a monthly automatic task. Inquiries still under review are not automatically deleted, to avoid accidental loss. Information used to block abusive reports is retained only for server security. Where retention is required by law, information may be kept for the required period.",
  "privacyContactTitle": "8. Policy changes and contact",
  "privacyContactBody": "If our data processing practices change, we will update this policy and its effective date. For requests to access or delete your information, app errors, usage questions or other inquiries, contact iccardreader10@gmail.com. Public policy: https://yohan020.github.io/ic_card_reader/privacy-en.html",
  "privacyEffectiveDate": "Effective date: October 27, 2026",
