  "passSource001": "Kyoto City Transportation Bureau subway fares",
  "passSource002": "Kyoto Open Data: 京都市営地下鉄 駅間距離・運賃",
  "passSource003": "Adapted from 京都市営地下鉄 駅間距離・運賃 (Kyoto City), CC BY 4.0. The one-day pass is valid until the end of service on the day of use. Transfers to other operators, discounts and child fares are excluded.",
  "passSource004": "Adapted from 京都市営地下鉄 駅間距離・運賃 (Kyoto City), CC BY 4.0. Bus routes, operators, variable-fare sections, late-night surcharges and excluded routes are not checked automatically.",
  "passSource005": "Only journeys covered by the selected pass are included, using adult basic fares for 301 stations and 45,150 station pairs. Designated buses use only fares entered manually after confirming eligibility.",
  "passSource006": "Looks up adult basic fares for 310 JR Hokkaido stations. Verified limited-express station pairs offer ordinary-car reserved-seat fares. JR Hokkaido Bus uses an estimate of ¥300 per ride, multiplied by the number entered.",
  "passSource007": "Looks up 1,260 directional adult regular fares between 36 physical stations on the device. Interchange line codes at Nakasu-Kawabata and Hakata are grouped into one physical station to avoid duplicate calculations.",
  "passSource008": "Looks up 1,406 directional adult IC/contactless fares between 38 stops on the device. Showamachi-dori serves only the Akasako direction, so departure and arrival directions are distinguished.",
  "passSource009": "Calculates adult regular fares using adjacent operating distances between 46 physical stations and official distance bands. Sapporo and Odori each count as one physical station, regardless of interchange lines.",
  "passSource010": "Applies the adult regular fare of ¥240 when two different stops among 77 stops are selected. Each journey entered counts as one separately charged ride.",
